{% set tool_name = namespace.tools.get("bash_tool_name") or "bash" %}
{% set view_tool = namespace.tools.get("view_tool_name") %}
{% set str_replace_tool = namespace.tools.get("str_replace_tool_name") %}
{% set create_tool = namespace.tools.get("create_tool_name") %}
{% set insert_tool = namespace.tools.get("insert_tool_name") %}
{# text_editor expands to leaf tools (view/str_replace/create/insert); also accept the wrapper name. #}
{% set has_text_editor = namespace.tools.get("has_text_editor") or view_tool or str_replace_tool or create_tool or insert_tool %}
{% set has_present_files = namespace.tools.get("has_present_files") %}
{% set present_files_tool = namespace.tools.get("present_files_tool_name") %}
{% set has_present_server = namespace.tools.get("has_present_server") %}
{% set present_server_tool = namespace.tools.get("present_server_tool_name") %}
{% if layout is not defined or not layout %}{% else %}
{% set workspace = layout | selectattr("name", "equalto", "user") | first %}
{% set outputs = layout | selectattr("name", "equalto", "outputs") | first %}
{% set uploads = layout | selectattr("name", "equalto", "uploads") | first %}
<{{ tool_name }}>
Execute shell commands in an isolated sandbox environment.

**Filesystem layout:**
| Path | Access | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
{% for mount in layout -%}
| `{{ mount.target }}` | {{ mount.access }} | {{ mount.description }} |
{% endfor %}
Rules:
- Use absolute paths. `{{ workspace.target }}` is the working directory.
- Do not access paths outside the directories listed above.
- Create intermediate work under `{{ workspace.target }}`.
- Save every deliverable the user should receive under `{{ outputs.target }}`.
{% if has_text_editor -%}
- Prefer the file tools for reading/editing text files{% if view_tool or str_replace_tool or create_tool or insert_tool %}: {% if view_tool %}`{{ view_tool }}` (read){% endif %}{% if str_replace_tool %}{% if view_tool %}, {% endif %}`{{ str_replace_tool }}` (edit){% endif %}{% if create_tool %}{% if view_tool or str_replace_tool %}, {% endif %}`{{ create_tool }}` (new file){% endif %}{% if insert_tool %}{% if view_tool or str_replace_tool or create_tool %}, {% endif %}`{{ insert_tool }}` (insert lines){% endif %}{% endif %}. Use `{{ tool_name }}` for shell work, builds, installs, and non-text files.
{% endif -%}
{% if has_present_files %}
**CRITICAL — delivering files to the user (`{{ present_files_tool }}`):**
- Writing a file is NOT enough. Files never appear in the chat UI unless you call `{{ present_files_tool }}`.
- After creating or updating any user-facing deliverable (reports, CSVs, images, PDFs, zips, code, charts, exports, etc.), you MUST call `{{ present_files_tool }}` with the absolute path(s) under `{{ outputs.target }}`.
- Call `{{ present_files_tool }}` in the same turn once the files are ready — do not only mention paths in prose.
- Prefer batching: pass every finished deliverable path in one `{{ present_files_tool }}` call.
- If you revise a deliverable, write the new version to `{{ outputs.target }}` and call `{{ present_files_tool }}` again.
- Never claim the user can download or open a file unless you already called `{{ present_files_tool }}` successfully for that path.
{% else -%}
- Save any file the user should receive to `{{ outputs.target }}`.
{% endif -%}
{% if has_present_server %}
**Exposing running services (`{{ present_server_tool }}`):**
- After starting an HTTP service in the sandbox (web app, Streamlit, Jupyter, etc.), call `{{ present_server_tool }}` with the port so the user gets a clickable URL.
- Starting the process alone does not surface a link; `{{ present_server_tool }}` is required.
{% endif -%}
{% if few_shots == "True" %}
Examples:
- Read an upload: `cat {{ uploads.target }}report.csv`
- Write a deliverable: `cp analysis.png {{ outputs.target }}analysis.png`
{% if has_present_files -%}
- Then present it: call `{{ present_files_tool }}` with `["{{ outputs.target }}analysis.png"]`
- Multiple outputs: write `{{ outputs.target }}summary.md` and `{{ outputs.target }}data.csv`, then call `{{ present_files_tool }}` once with both absolute paths
{% endif -%}
{% if has_present_server -%}
- Started a server on port 8501: call `{{ present_server_tool }}` with port `8501` (optional `initial_path`)
{% endif -%}
{% if has_text_editor and view_tool -%}
- Read a text file: call `{{ view_tool }}` with path `{{ workspace.target }}notes.md`
{% endif -%}
{% endif %}
</{{ tool_name }}>
{% endif %}
